{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Joseph died, and all his brothers, and all that generation.</b> Reuven was born on the 14th of Kislev and died at the age of 125 years. Shimon was born on the 21st of Tevet and died at the age of 120 years. Levi was born on the 16th of Nisan and died at the age of 137 years. Yehudah was born on the 15th of Sivan and died at the age of 119 years. Dan was born on the 9th of Elul and died at the age of 125 years. Naftali was born on the 5th of Tishrei and died at the age of 133 years. Gad was born on the 10th of Marcheshvan and died at the age of 125 years. Asher was born on the 20th of Shevat and died at the age of 123 years. Yissachar was born on the 10th of Av and died at the age of 122 years. Zevulun was born on the 7th of Tishrei and died at the age of 114 years. Yosef was born on the 1st of Tammuz and died at the age of 110 years. Binyamin was born on the 11th of Marcheshvan and died at the age of 109 years. In Adar and in Iyar none were born; these were left for Ephraim and Menasheh. I found this in Midrash Tadshea. <b>And Joseph died, and all his brothers, and all that generation.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even though Joseph died, their Elohim endured, as it is said, ״וימת יוסף,״ and immediately after it, ״ובני ישראל פרו וישרצו וירבו ויעצמו במאד מאד״ — Scripture teaches you that before the enslavement, this blessing of swarming and mightiness was sent among them; and after the enslavement began, it diminished from the swarming and the mightiness, and there remained among them only fruitfulness and multiplication. And this is what it says: ״וכאשר יענו אותו כן ירבה וכן יפרוץ״ — as they afflicted them, so did they multiply and so did they spread." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> ״ובני ישראל פרו וישרצו״ — they were fruitful; what is distinctive about this? Scripture says וישרצו — six in one womb, like these sheratzim (swarming creatures). One might think they were lowly like sheratzim — Scripture says וירבו — of tall stature. One might think they were weak — Scripture says ויעצמו — mighty. במאד מאד — 'exceedingly' in this world, 'exceedingly' in the world to come, as it is said (Isaiah 49:21): ״ואמרת בלבבך מי ילד לי את אלה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:12.076748528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}